+### Post-review reporter fixes — 2026-10-05
+
+The fresh-context review identified reporter edge cases after the original
+T13/T14 validation. They were fixed in separate commits:
+
+| Commit | Change |
+| --- | --- |
+| `b19a1b75` | JUnit, SonarQube, TeamCity, and TAP report exhausted unexpected `[!shouldfail]` passes and accepted failures from the final logical outcome. |
+| `0dd78e55` | Machine-readable reporters preserve missing-assertion failures and superseded diagnostics when no assertion event is emitted. |
+| `5669b8e6` | Console and compact report final skipped and accepted outcomes accurately. |
+| `30ab6617` | JUnit retry-enabled suite counters count final logical test cases and distinguish errors from failures. |
+
+After these changes, the regenerated sources and configured Windows builds
+were validated again. The focused reporter/amalgamation group passed 5/5,
+`all` passed 157/157, and `basic` passed 92/92. No unapproved approval-test
+baselines were produced; the only build warnings were the four known MSVC
+`D9025` warnings from disabled-exceptions targets. `git diff --check` passed.
+All 18 exported patches applied to a clean `v3.16.0` worktree and produced
+tree `8c8ac8df7cde538ceeb80dd299baec31103bf847`, matching commit `30ab6617`.
+
 ## 9. Known limitations and unsupported cases
 
 - Catch2 does not roll back test-owned or external state: globals, statics,
diff --git a/docs/reporters.md b/docs/reporters.md
index 1bc7b92b..f47e66f9 100644
--- a/docs/reporters.md
+++ b/docs/reporters.md
@@ -50,9 +50,11 @@ representations are:
 | Automake | Writes one result line for the logical test case, based on its final outcome. |
 
 With retries disabled, reporter output is unchanged. With retries enabled but
-unused, only XML and JSON add structural attempt information. TAP buffers its
-own lines until an attempt ends, so those lines can interleave differently
-with output written directly by the test; the TAP text itself is unchanged.
+unused, XML and JSON add structural attempt information. Accepted failures
+(`[!mayfail]` or an expected failure under `[!shouldfail]`) are represented
+as skipped in JUnit and marked `TODO` in TAP, even when no additional attempt
+runs. TAP buffers its own lines until an attempt ends, so those lines can
+interleave differently with output written directly by the test.
 
 Custom reporters can observe attempts through the
 [`testCaseAttempt` events](reporter-events.md#testcaseattempt-events).
